# W-B-Q1, a window(a, b) in added: L4_2_schedule_added_window's rule, over every day the window can take (L §4.2:
# "every day known but one"). d3: Monday 2026-06-22, rolled following, is 06-23 where the added day is 06-22 and 06-22
# where it is any other day of window(2026-06-19, 2026-06-23); so its day is window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23), though
# at the window's first and last day it is 06-22 both times (L §4.4 "give the interval of their values at its first
# and last day": HANDOVER contradiction 46). d4: the business day after Thursday 2026-06-18 is Friday 06-19 unless the
# added day is 06-19, then Monday 06-22.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar
input pay_dom: int

ask d3: schedule(2026-06, pay_dom, following, len) law 2026-06-01
ask d4: add_business(2026-06-18, 1, len)

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [window(2026-06-19, 2026-06-23)])
  pay_dom = 22 "own"
=== expect
d3: window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23)
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-12-31
d4: window(2026-06-19, 2026-06-22)
  cut 2026-12-31
